prompt:
A real photograph, taken with a good phone camera and looking exactly like a phone photograph, of the common room of a care home for elderly people at coffee time on a sunny afternoon, taken by a carer standing near the door, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus from the floor in the foreground to the back wall. Natural colours, warm afternoon light from the large windows. The textures of real wood, fabric, porcelain, paper, plastic, steel and skin, with the true depth and the slight lens perspective of a photograph.

Every object and every person stands on its own, with a little space around them, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. The whole room carries no writing, numbers, print, symbol or logo anywhere: the newspaper shows only grey blocks and a photograph, the calendar on the wall shows only a painting of flowers above a plain grid of empty squares, the large wall clock has a plain cream face with only twelve short black tick marks, and the room looks as it could look in any care home in Europe or America.

THE TABLE fills the middle of the picture: a light oak dining table with a white tablecloth, seen from its end, with four wooden chairs with armrests and green seat cushions. On the table, each thing apart from the others:
- a white porcelain coffee pot;
- four white cups on saucers;
- a round plate with a plum cake cut into squares, and a cake server beside it;
- a photo album lying open, its two pages showing small old black-and-white photographs of a tram and of a young man in a uniform cap;
- a folded newspaper;
- a box of a jigsaw puzzle with a picture of a lighthouse on its lid, and a few puzzle pieces spread beside it;
- a pair of reading glasses lying folded.

THE RESIDENTS:
- On the left of the table, sitting in an armchair-like chair: an old man of about eighty-seven, tall and thin, with a long friendly face, thick white hair combed to the side, big ears, a small white beard and bright blue eyes, in a grey cardigan over a checked flannel shirt and dark-brown trousers. A small skin-coloured hearing aid shows behind his ear. He leans on the table with one forearm and looks down at the photo album with a dreamy smile, the index finger of his other hand resting on the photograph of the tram.
- On the right of the table, facing him: an old woman of about eighty-one, small and round, with short white curly hair, pink cheeks and pearl earrings, in a lilac twin-set, holding her coffee cup in both hands and laughing.
- At the far end of the table, in a grey care wheelchair with a high padded backrest and a padded headrest, an old woman of about ninety with thin white hair in a bun and a soft blue blanket over her knees, looking at the cake with a peaceful face.

AROUND THE TABLE:
- beside the old man's chair, on the left of the picture, a grey four-wheeled rollator walking frame with its brakes on and its small basket empty;
- on the floor in front of the table, a soft red rubber ball the size of a melon;
- on the right of the picture, against the wall, a small white drinks station: a narrow white table with a glass jug of water, a glass jug of orange juice and a stack of plastic cups;
- along the right-hand wall, at hip height, a long round wooden handrail fixed to the wall on steel brackets.

THE BACK WALL: two large windows with white frames showing a garden with trees and a lawn; between them, a large round wall clock with a plain cream face and twelve short black tick marks, mounted high; to the left of the windows, the wall calendar with a painting of flowers. A large green potted plant stands on the floor in the corner by the windows.

The floor is warm light wooden laminate, the walls are soft warm white. The bottom of the picture shows the floor in front of the table and the red ball. The moment is cosy and cheerful.
